mac80211_hwsim: allow wmediumd to register with channels > 1

Stock mac80211_hwsim rejects HWSIM_CMD_REGISTER with -EOPNOTSUPP whenever the
radio pool was loaded with channels > 1. The guard is precautionary ("userspace
multi-channel behaviour not asserted safe"), not a hard limitation: the kernel
<-> wmediumd protocol already carries per-frame frequency (HWSIM_ATTR_FREQ), and
a channels-aware wmediumd (see gen/wmediumd) handles the concurrent contexts.

This is the single change that lets the EasyMesh lab run FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY
(concurrent 2.4 GHz ch6 + 5 GHz ch36 on one phy, needing channels>=2) *under*
wmediumd for a real RF gradient, instead of dropping to a 5 GHz-only channels=1
medium. Downgrade the refusal to a one-shot warning.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim.c
@@ -5769,7 +5769,7 @@
 	 * For current userspace, prohibit it since it won't work right.
 	 */
 	if (chans > 1)
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		pr_warn("mac80211_hwsim: EXPERIMENTAL wmediumd with %u channels\n", chans);

 	if (hwsim_net_get_wmediumd(net))
 		return -EBUSY;
